# Development

The app and the landing site are two packages in one pnpm workspace. The app is SvelteKit with a Node or Vercel adapter. The landing site is a static SvelteKit build.

## Setup

Node.js 26.13.0 and pnpm 12.16.1 are pinned in `package.json`. Use pnpm only; do not create a second lockfile.

<CopyCommand command="pnpm install --frozen-lockfile" />

Copy the development environment example:

<CopyCommand command="cp .env.development.example .env.development" />

Leave the Turso values blank for a local SQLite file. `pnpm dev` loads `.env.development`.

## App

<CopyCommand command="pnpm dev" />

The app runs on the Vite port. The packaged app uses `pnpm start` or `pnpm start:local`.

## Landing and docs

The landing site lives in `landing/`. Its docs are `.svx` pages under `landing/src/routes/docs/`.

<CopyCommand command="pnpm dev:landing" />

Open `http://localhost:5174/docs`. `APP_URL` falls back to `http://localhost:5174`; set it when you need the public install URLs:

<CopyCommand command="APP_URL=https://your-landing.vercel.app pnpm build:landing" />

On Windows PowerShell:

<CopyCommand command="$env:APP_URL = 'https://your-landing.vercel.app'; pnpm build:landing" />

The landing Vercel project uses the `landing` directory as its root, runs `pnpm install` from the repository root and builds with `pnpm build:landing`. Set `APP_URL` in its project environment or the build fails.

## Gates

The inner loop checks only changed files:

<CopyCommand command="pnpm lint:changed && pnpm typecheck:changed && pnpm test:changed" />

Run the full gate before a merge:

<CopyCommand
	command="pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck && pnpm test && pnpm build && pnpm build:landing && pnpm budget && pnpm test:smoke && pnpm test:package && pnpm audit:gate"
/>

Run `pnpm budget` alone, not in parallel with other heavy commands. `pnpm test:package` packs the npm tarball, installs it in a temporary directory and checks local and deployed login.

## Docker image

CI builds the image after the gates pass on `main` and publishes it to GitHub Container Registry. A local build is still useful when changing the Dockerfile:

<CopyCommand command="docker build -t last30days-news ." />

## Branches and releases

- Branch per phase, feature or fix; small docs edits can go directly to `main`.
- Merge with `--no-ff` and keep the branch.
- Commits follow Conventional Commits.
- Semantic release runs on green `main` CI. GitHub releases always; npm publishes only when `NPM_TOKEN` is in the `release` environment.

Read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/Emmraan/last30days-news/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) before a pull request.

